From cea1aacc924338035cacd452f9c27cf2ddc850e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:17:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [depends] libdvdread, libdvdnav: fixes from their master
 branches

libdvdread 7.1.1 and libdvdnav 7.0.0 are their latest releases. The
commits below of their master branches on code.videolan.org go on top
as tools/depends patches, listed in the cmake modules and Makefiles
after the existing patches (for libdvdread, after the Kodi patches 01,
02 and 09). Each is the upstream git format-patch of its commit, with
its author, date and message, except two libdvdread backports that say
what differs in a "Hades:" line.

Kodi plays a DVD through libdvdnav (CDVDInputStreamNavigator); its own
code calls no libdvdread function. libdvdnav reaches DVDOpen and
DVDOpenStream, ifoOpen*, ifoRead_* (TT_SRPT, VTS_PTT_SRPT, PGCIT,
PGCI_UT, VOBU_ADMAP, ...), DVDReadBlocks, navRead_PCI/DSI and the UDF
and ISO volume info. With kodi-9204, libdvdread treats every medium as
DVD-Video for Kodi, so its DVD-Audio and DVD-VR paths are not reached.

libdvdnav (round 1, unchanged):
- 03 5aaa457e  Fixed dvdnav_cell_find for cell boundary (seeking to the
               very end works again)
- 04 2ffc50b5  NULL dereference of cell_playback in play_Cell and
               play_Cell_post on a PGC with cells but no cell table

libdvdread, in master order (22 to 24 were round 1's two; ce9bdb7 and
the master order put them at the end):
- 10 f5cdeae9  DVDReadBlocks dereferenced dvd_file before checking it
- 11 534350c1  navRead_PCI zero-fills the structure before parsing; in
               7.1.1 pci_t is still packed (07da473 is later), so this
               only hardens, as upstream does
- 12 c012dd88  document the return values of UDFGetAVDP
- 13 602cb1d3  UDFGetAVDP returns only 0 or 1
- 14 99dc1062  UDFMapICB, UDFScanDir, UDFFindPartition and
               UDFGetDescriptor return 0 on a read error, not the
               negative read result their callers took for success
- 15 172ca84c  UDFFindFile returns 0 on a read error, not a negative
               value turned into a block number
- 16 92f3a6e5  DVDReadLBUDF returns ssize_t  [backport]
- 17 918878e0  UDFGetAVDP passes the read error on, and its two callers
               check for <= 0
- 18 c1de9313  read the PTT entries without an unaligned cast
- 19 f1e207f5  don't read PTT entries past the end of the buffer
- 20 788a5afd  a PATH_MAX path written into a smaller buffer in
               cppm_get_mkb_or_backup (DVD-Audio, so not reached by
               Kodi; a stack overflow fix, taken as listed)
- 21 5bfb2efc  bound the fallback directory path in findDVDFile
               [backport]
- 22 ce9bdb77  when the partition or volume is not in the main volume
               descriptor sequence, read the backup one from the AVDP
               (the fallback read the main one again)
- 23 636a8e2c  avoid a large or negative info_length from read data
- 24 09530764  error if the VOBU_ADMAP last_byte is too small

14 to 17 close, in libdvdread itself, the read-error path that
kodi-9204 describes for a folder read as an image (UDFGetAVDP returned
the negative error and UDFFindPartition, testing only for 0, went on
with a location never filled in). kodi-9204 stays: it makes
DVDProbeType() answer DVD-Video for Kodi, which these commits do not
change. Without it 7.1 still opens the medium once more to probe and
reads a DVD-Video disc that also carries a DVD-VR folder as DVD-VR.

The two backports:
- 16: 7.1.1 rewrote DVDReadLBUDF, so the hunk for its body does not
  apply; the same return-type change is made to 7.1.1's body.
- 21: upstream changes the two-sprintf findDVDFile of 2a6d7b9 (a later
  rewrite, not taken); 7.1.1's findDVDFile has four unbounded
  sprintf(video_path, ...) and all four become snprintf with
  sizeof(video_path), which is what the commit does.

Not taken, every other master commit since 7.1.1 that touches src/
(master 0f30df53125b, checked with ls-remote), with the fact:
- 50009a0 (find the file set descriptor through the logical volume
  descriptor): it fixes images whose FSD is not at the start of the
  partition, but it accepts a volume only when the FSD's partition
  reference number (long_ad, bytes 8-9) equals the partition
  descriptor's partition number (bytes 22-23). ECMA-167 makes these
  different fields; they agree on usual DVDs, where both are 0. A disc
  with another partition number would stop opening, and the media
  test that would show it cannot run here (below). Not taken blind.
- 5a93cda (DVDDiscID return value): neither libdvdnav nor Kodi calls
  DVDDiscID.
- 5ad3046 (stream type before the title key): 7.1.1 creates each
  device as DVD_V and css_title() changes only for DVD_A/DVD_VR; with
  DVD-Video only, the order cannot matter.
- 21ba2d4 (dvdinput function pointers per reader, not global): with
  libdvdcss linked (-Dlibdvdcss=enabled sets HAVE_DVDCSS_DVDCSS_H),
  every reader sets the same pointers.
- c32b0dd (dlclose of a NULL handle): only in the dlopen path, which
  the linked build does not compile.
- de61288, 228ddaa, 3417c8f, 60ee58f, 85296dd, 58d5c6e, d6f94f7,
  c8bf871, 4749724 and the DVD-Audio field, layout and comment
  changes: DVD-Audio paths.
- d824fe6 (32-bit off_t), 1c2c33e and other Windows, wasm, OS/2 and
  bswap fallback changes: not compiled for Linux x86_64.
- 2a6d7b9, b409628 and the zone-directory follow-ups: a feature and
  its follow-ups. d0a7af1 (strcpy for sprintf), 8ddc0b4: cosmetic, and
  d0a7af1 does not apply to 7.1.1.
- 12916a3, 07da473 and the other packing changes: they change the
  layout of public structures (btin_t, hli_t, pci_t) that libdvdnav
  7.0.0 is built against, an ABI change rather than a fix;
- static_assert and the bitreader compile-time checks (e2bc9c9,
  daa9277, d30059e), the nav_read/bitreader refactors, documentation
  and warning fixes: no change at run time.

Checked:
- the 15 libdvdread patches apply to the archive the recipe hands Kodi
  (libdvdread-7.1.1.tar.xz, SHA256 as the recipe) after 01, 02 and 09,
  in order, with patch -p1 --fuzz=0 (line offsets only), and the files
  they touch then equal those of a git worktree with the same commits
  cherry-picked on the 7.1.1 tag; the libdvdnav ones as in round 1;
- built the way FindLibDvdRead.cmake builds it (meson, static,
  release, -D_XBMC) with the LibreELEC Generic target compiler: it
  compiles with the same warnings as without the series, the objects
  that change are dvd_reader, dvd_udf, ifo_read and nav_read, and
  libdvdnav 7.0.0 (with 03, 04) builds against it.
- Not run: the DVD playback test. Its
  media tools (dvdauthor, genisoimage, and the system meson, ninja and
  pkg-config it calls) were removed from the distro when that check
  closed, and nothing is installed here.
