diff --git a/tools/depends/target/libdvdread/21-all-dvd_reader-bound-directory-path.patch b/tools/depends/target/libdvdread/21-all-dvd_reader-bound-directory-path.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bca64a4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/depends/target/libdvdread/21-all-dvd_reader-bound-directory-path.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+From 5bfb2efce92810e7c327edbdbfdabb298e5fb187 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Jean-Baptiste Kempf <jb@kyber.tech>
+Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:05:20 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] dvd_reader: bound the directory path formatting
+
+findDVDFile builds a fallback path with sprintf("%s/%s/", path_root,
+subdir) into a PATH_MAX+1 buffer. path_root comes from the caller's
+directory and is never length-checked, so a near-PATH_MAX path overflows
+the stack buffer by the length of the subdirectory. Use snprintf, like
+the sibling path building already does.
+
+The two lines were rewritten in 2a6d7b9 (the unbounded write itself is
+older).
+
+Fixes: 2a6d7b9bf751 ("findDVDFile: allow selecting the zone directory explicitly")
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+(cherry picked from commit 5bfb2efce92810e7c327edbdbfdabb298e5fb187)
+
+Hades: upstream changes a later two-sprintf findDVDFile (after 2a6d7b9,
+not taken); 7.1.1 has four unbounded sprintf(video_path, ...) in that
+function and all four become snprintf with sizeof(video_path), as the
+commit does.
+---
+ src/dvd_reader.c | 8 ++++----
+ 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/src/dvd_reader.c b/src/dvd_reader.c
+index 9393c6f7ed43..b13e952ac041 100644
+--- a/src/dvd_reader.c
++++ b/src/dvd_reader.c
+@@ -977,22 +977,22 @@ static int findDVDFile( dvd_reader_t *dvd, const char *file, char *filename )
+ 
+     /* Try also with adding the path, just in case. */
